  "details": "If there is at least one VRC_Storage component in the world, no other users’ voice will be heard for about 6 seconds after entering the world, and VRC_Trigger components will not work.\nThis issue has not occured, at least in Unity 2017.4.\nThis issue may be related to https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/921-vrcdatastorage-completely-breaks-vrctrigger-vrchat-202011p3\n \nDemo scenes:\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/511077066628661271/719129350473252905/VRC_DataStorage-lag-test.unitypackage\n \nDemo worlds:\n[VRC_DataStorage exsit] https://www.vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_ba99feeb-49d5-4f44-9e9d-925b7393aaf6\n[VRC_DataStorage do not exsit] https://www.vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_0f8212e0-8c92-49b1-9a55-1a5e0567e12a\n \nYou can work around this issue by deactivating the GameObject that contains VRC_DataStorage components, activating it about 2 seconds after entering the world.\nhttps://www.vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_9e00ff67-cd98-468f-9521-f73fc5dd33e4\n \nHowever, Oculus Quest can only display VRC_Panorama, which is enabled by default, due to the following issue existing in VRC_Panorama.\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/842-vrcpanorama-not-function-properly-for-quest-users",
